    <node id="漢代學術思想">
      <data key="d0">漢代學術思想</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">漢代的學術思想受到孔子及其儒學的影響，對中國的文化傳承至關重要。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5203ee952df2751a57e4aa3f1835f80b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="周易">
      <data key="d0">周易</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《周易》, also known as the I Ching, is an ancient Chinese text that explores the concepts of change, philosophy, and the relationships between different entities, profoundly influencing Chinese culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="伏羲氏">
      <data key="d0">伏羲氏</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">伏羲氏, also known as Fuxi, is a legendary figure in Chinese mythology attributed with the creation of the eight trigrams that form the basis of the I Ching's divination system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="周文王">
      <data key="d0">周文王</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">周文王, or King Wen of Zhou, is credited with expanding upon the I Ching by adding the 64 hexagrams and composing the accompanying text known as the 'Yao' statements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="商朝">
      <data key="d0">商朝</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">商朝, or the Shang Dynasty, is the historical period during which the divination methods related to the I Ching are believed to have originated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="周朝">
      <data key="d0">周朝</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">周朝, or the Zhou Dynasty, is the dynasty during which significant developments in the I Ching's content and interpretation occurred.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="十翼">
      <data key="d0">十翼</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">十翼 encompasses the ten commentaries that elaborate on the text of the I Ching, providing interpretations of its teachings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="六十四卦">
      <data key="d0">六十四卦</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">六十四卦 are the 64 hexagrams described in the I Ching that represent various situations and changes in the world.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="卦辞">
      <data key="d0">卦辞</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">卦辞 refers to the text associated with each hexagram in the I Ching that provides guidance and interpretation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="爻辞">
      <data key="d0">爻辞</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">爻辞 are the specific lines associated with each hexagram, providing detailed meanings and insights for interpretation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e8108d72a5081f3d3f6a324e51fc6b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="王弼">
      <data key="d0">王弼</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">王弼是另一位魏晉學者，他將老莊思想與儒道義理融合來阐释经典内容。&lt;SEP&gt;王弼是西晋时期的学者，他注释了《易经》，该注释被后世广泛沿用，并对易学的发展产生了重大影响。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaec9998840144f5983cb2a67a706cdc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孔颖达">
      <data key="d0">孔颖达</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Kong Yingda was a scholar of the Tang Dynasty who created the commentary '礼记正义', impacting the understanding of '礼记'.&lt;SEP&gt;孔颖达是唐代著名的学者，编纂了《五经正义》，对《易经》的理解和传播具有重要贡献。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61c1e6a8981e6c1f6d0fa734c2df7c7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="程颖">
      <data key="d0">程颖</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">程颖是宋代著名的易学家，他创作了《易程传》，对易学的重要性进行阐述。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="朱熹">
      <data key="d0">朱熹</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Zhu Xi is a prominent Confucian scholar whose interpretations of '礼记' elevated its importance in the context of examination culture during the Song Dynasty.&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹 is a prominent Neo-Confucian leader who played a significant role in elevating the status of Mencius' work within the Confucian canon.&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹 was a prominent Confucian scholar during the Southern Song dynasty who elevated the status of 《孟子》 and other texts in the Confucian canon.&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是南宋著名的儒學家，他的《四書章句集注》對《論語》和《孟子》的理解和詮釋做出了重要貢獻。&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是宋代的哲学家，他的《周易正义》对理解《易经》及其哲学思想有深远影响。&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是著名的儒學家，著作有《四書章句集注》，對儒學及《孟子》有深遠影響。&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是宋代的理學家，他對《春秋》及其解釋有深入的貢獻。&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是宋代著名的理學家，他的著作《朱子語類》提到《春秋經》的要義及其歷史價值。&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹 was a prominent neo-Confucian scholar known for his interpretations of Confucian classics, especially his influential work on The Four Books.&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是南宋時期的儒學家，其作品《四書章句集注》對《論語》的學習有深遠影響。&lt;SEP&gt;朱熹是南宋時期的儒學家，其作品《四書章句集注》對《論語》的學習有著深遠影響。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bccd7f74cfb40acfe435a9254b38710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61c1e6a8981e6c1f6d0fa734c2df7c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ddf53d87bd692aeb35a6718692c1d26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e8683900122ec6ae46cbdea0097760d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153bf19155c06ea022c365c26c3f7bd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d45d81c047e5d9ed7e6262bdc870be</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《周易》">
      <data key="d0">《周易》</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">《周易》, also known as the Book of Changes, is a pivotal text in Confucian philosophy studied for its insights into metaphysics and ethics.&lt;SEP&gt;《周易》是中国古代经典之一，被视为哲学与占卜的结合，具备重要的文化和学术价值。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e8683900122ec6ae46cbdea0097760d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《五经正义》">
      <data key="d0">《五经正义》</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《五经正义》是孔颖达编纂的一部集大成的经典注释书，系统阐述了五经的义理，包括《周易》。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《易程传》">
      <data key="d0">《易程传》</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《易程传》由程颖撰写，是对《易经》及其理论的深入分析和总结。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《周易正义》">
      <data key="d0">《周易正义》</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《周易正义》是朱熹的重要著作，注重对《周易》哲学的探讨。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
    </node>
    <node id="《日知录》">
      <data key="d0">《日知录》</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">《日知录》由顾炎武撰写，涉及对《易经》的评论及其实际应用。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-114ae7417f2464f12b59d413a2a9ef94</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
