    <edge source="五经" target="论语">
      <data key="d5">17.0</data>
      <data key="d6">The Analects is considered to be part of the Five Classics, further solidifying its essential role in the literary and philosophical landscape of Confucianism.&lt;SEP&gt;《论语》与《五经》之间的关系在于两者都是儒家经典，而《论语》在汉代时开始逐渐被认同为经典的一部分。</data>
      <data key="d7">literary significance, classic composition&lt;SEP&gt;经典承认，文化地位</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="五经" target="孟子">
      <data key="d5">18.0</data>
      <data key="d6">Mencius’s eventual incorporation into the list of Five Classics represents a significant development in recognizing its philosophical importance in Confucianism.&lt;SEP&gt;《孟子》作为儒家经典之一，最终在南宋时被正式纳入经典，与《五经》共同构成了儒家传统的核心。</data>
      <data key="d7">classic recognition, philosophical value&lt;SEP&gt;经典地位，文化传承</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="论语" target="汉代">
      <data key="d5">15.0</data>
      <data key="d6">During the Han Dynasty, the Analects was recognized as an essential educational text that shaped the curriculum for scholars, marking its growing significance in Chinese studies.&lt;SEP&gt;汉代对《论语》的地位提升，使其在教育体系中被视为重要教材，反映了其经典地位。</data>
      <data key="d7">historical influence, education reform&lt;SEP&gt;历史时期，教育影响</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="论语" target="四书">
      <data key="d5">9.0</data>
      <data key="d6">The Analects is one of the Four Books, which are foundational texts in Confucianism that have been critical in Chinese educational systems since the Yuan Dynasty.</data>
      <data key="d7">classical texts, educational significance</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="论语" target="唐代">
      <data key="d5">8.0</data>
      <data key="d6">In the Tang Dynasty, the Analects was firmly integrated into the educational canon, showcasing its established role in the scholarly tradition of Confucianism.</data>
      <data key="d7">educational establishment, Confucian tradition</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="论语" target="孔子">
      <data key="d5">10.0</data>
      <data key="d6">Confucius is the central figure behind the teachings found in the Analects, fundamentally linking his philosophy to this text's significance in Confucian education.</data>
      <data key="d7">philosophical foundation, educational impact</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="唐代">
      <data key="d5">14.0</data>
      <data key="d6">During the Tang Dynasty, figures like Han Yu advocated for Mencius, highlighting its growing acceptance and importance in Confucian studies.&lt;SEP&gt;在唐代，虽然《孟子》未被纳入经部，但其被提倡和讨论的情况显示出社会对其的重视。</data>
      <data key="d7">advocacy, cultural significance&lt;SEP&gt;文化提倡，社会重视</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="宋代">
      <data key="d5">17.0</data>
      <data key="d6">In the Song Dynasty, Mencius was formally canonized into classic texts, reflecting its increased importance in Confucian thought at that time.&lt;SEP&gt;宋代鹰视《孟子》的地位提升，最终将其正式纳入经典之一，表明了其在儒家学派中的重要性。</data>
      <data key="d7">textual recognition, philosophical elevation&lt;SEP&gt;经典承认，教育进步</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="四书">
      <data key="d5">9.0</data>
      <data key="d6">Mencius is another significant component of the Four Books, crucial for understanding Confucian philosophical principles alongside the Analects.</data>
      <data key="d7">classical texts, philosophical importance</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="汉代">
      <data key="d5">7.0</data>
      <data key="d6">In the Han Dynasty, Mencius's status began to ascend, but it did not achieve the same level of recognition as the Analects until much later periods.</data>
      <data key="d7">historical context, educational status</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="王允">
      <data key="d5">7.0</data>
      <data key="d6">Wang Yun's endorsement of Mencius during the Han Dynasty contributed significantly to its recognition in educational curricula.</data>
      <data key="d7">advocacy, historical significance</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="韩愈">
      <data key="d5">8.0</data>
      <data key="d6">Han Yu's support for Mencius during the Tang Dynasty illustrated the growing respect and interest in Mencius's work and its philosophical contributions.</data>
      <data key="d7">cultural advocacy, intellectual growth</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-c02f96884f421f06d459abb266d91550</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="儒家">
      <data key="d5">9.0</data>
      <data key="d6">《孟子》延續了儒家思想，並對後世的道德觀念有影響。</data>
      <data key="d7">經典, 衍生</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-a563a3e23fade380d6ab321c1b3ee82c</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="《孟子》">
      <data key="d5">19.0</data>
      <data key="d6">孟子 developed the content and philosophy that is recorded in the text 《孟子》, representing his teachings.&lt;SEP&gt;孟子 is the author and central figure presented in 《孟子》, which contains his teachings and philosophical discourse.</data>
      <data key="d7">authorship, philosophical work&lt;SEP&gt;philosopher, authored works</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-80d45d81c047e5d9ed7e6262bdc870be</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="孔子">
      <data key="d5">54.0</data>
      <data key="d6">Mencius built upon Confucius' foundational teachings, integrating and expanding them into his own philosophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Mencius built upon the teachings of Confucius, emphasizing and expanding his ethical principles.&lt;SEP&gt;《孟子》作為儒家經典之一，繼承和發展了孔子的思想。&lt;SEP&gt;《孟子》在許多方面延續了孔子的教導和理念，作為儒家經典之一與《論語》相輔相成。&lt;SEP&gt;孟子作為孔子的後繼者，繼承並發展了孔子對經學的整理和解釋。&lt;SEP&gt;孟子是孔子思想的追隨者，進一步發展了內聖外王的理論。</data>
      <data key="d7">philosophical development, legacy&lt;SEP&gt;philosophical influence, teaching lineage&lt;SEP&gt;philosophical lineage, influence&lt;SEP&gt;思想繼承, 教育&lt;SEP&gt;經典,傳承&lt;SEP&gt;經典,繼承</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-e06e41970449ac931423e76276bd2a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778f057ebbb3f89bd1278c6c6c69bc3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153bf19155c06ea022c365c26c3f7bd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d45d81c047e5d9ed7e6262bdc870be</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="漢書">
      <data key="d5">7.0</data>
      <data key="d6">《漢書》 documents the historical context and significance of Mencius' works, providing a reference for his contributions.</data>
      <data key="d7">historical documentation, scholarly reference</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-80d45d81c047e5d9ed7e6262bdc870be</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="孟子" target="萬章">
      <data key="d5">8.0</data>
